-C10 alkylcarbonyl; and R&lt;2&gt; is hydrogen, C1-C10 alkyl, or C2-C10 alkylcarbonyl, with the proviso that the cases wherein R&lt; alpha &gt; is C2-C10 alkylcarbonyl and both R&lt;1&gt; and R&lt;2&gt; are C1-C10 alkyl are excepted.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés représentés par la formule générale (I), ou des sels desdits composés. Dans ladite formule, R&lt; alpha &gt; représente C1-C10 alkyle, C3-C10 alcényle, C7-C15 aralkyle, quinoléinylalkyle, quinoléinylalcényle, C2-C10 alkylcarbonyle, C7-C15 aralkylcarbonyle, C4-C7 cycloalkylcarbonyle, benzoyle, imidazolylcarbonyle, ou analogue; R&lt;1&gt; représente hydrogène, C1-C10 alkyle ou C2-C10 alkylcarbonyle, exception étant faite des cas où R&lt; alpha &gt; représente C2-C10 alkylcarbonyle et où R&lt;1&gt; et R&lt;2&gt; désignent C1-C10 alkyle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>